    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "The full suite is green: **263 tests, 0 failures, 0 errors**.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the `capacityWarning` flag so that an owner's response reports `true` when the owner's city already holds between 40 and 49 owners (approaching the hard limit of 50), leaving the existing 50-owner hard rejection untouched.\n\nFollowing the codebase's existing pattern for read-time derived warnings (`bulkSignupWarning`), the changes were:\n\n1. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added a read-only `capacityWarning` boolean to the Owner schema, so the generated `OwnerDto` gets a `setCapacityWarning` setter.\n\n2. **`OwnerCityCapacity.java`** (new helper class, mirroring `OwnerBulkSignup`) \u2014 holds the shared, case-insensitive per-city count logic plus:\n   - `isAtCapacity(...)` \u2014 count \u2265 50 (the hard limit).\n   - `isWarning(...)` \u2014 count in [40, 49] (approaching, but not at, capacity).\n\n3. **`EnsureOwnerCityCapacity.java`** \u2014 refactored to delegate its hard-limit check to `OwnerCityCapacity.isAtCapacity(...)`, keeping its single public `service` method (required by the one-public-method-per-function rule \u2014 my first attempt at adding a second static method to this class broke start-up, which is why the logic moved to a helper).\n\n4. **The four responders** (`RespondWithOwner`, `RespondWithOwnerCreated`, `RespondWithOwnerUpdated`, `RespondWithExistingOwner`) \u2014 each now sets `dto.setCapacityWarning(OwnerCityCapacity.isWarning(...))`, so the flag surfaces on GET, POST-create, update, and idempotent-replay responses alike.\n\n5. **`OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 added `@Mapping(target = \"capacityWarning\", ignore = true)` so MapStruct leaves the derived field for the responders to populate.\n\nThe new `AcceptanceTest.coreWarnsWhenApproachingCapacity` passes, as does the entire existing suite.",
